{"id": "EUVD-2026-64411", "enisaUuid": "6af4e57b-be14-3ab9-95b5-51bce815dd3f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipvs: avoid out-of-bounds write in ip_vs_nat_icmp\n\nSashiko warns that local attacker can modify the packet\nwhile it is processed by IPVS. Some places read the\nIP ihl field multiple times which can cause out-of-bounds\naccess. One such place is ip_vs_nat_icmp where we\ncan write after the validated area.\n\nFix it by providing ciph argument just like it is done for\nIPv6 and use ciph->len as offset to the embedded transport\nheader.\n\nModify some IPv4 header checks by reading the ihl field\nonly once.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:33:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:16:11", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b8f79af0e98f27b932b0b416e9c52b692d31ff9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c779b258c9c3c3567af68d4f45c2f751f35bd0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/be65fa324640c7a95e30b146159a2be5cc73f22e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a69a4b3fff5814d079beff9a1e9d369994b2ed47", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/243d0187ec4c3837b9b0004f18d1068e46115760", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/646922a0379496154e8c8faca4f8e2fd9100cacc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74724", "GHSA-qcch-2r2r-xcw2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0259a556-f8a8-3040-acb3-538ddcc74e63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.183"}, {"id": "04040cb1-844d-3978-ad83-aa1de98dd637", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <a69a4b3fff5814d079beff9a1e9d369994b2ed47"}, {"id": "160a3b72-3eaa-36dc-b446-16564b358bfe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <3c779b258c9c3c3567af68d4f45c2f751f35bd0e"}, {"id": "341244e3-cd12-34d9-b6ba-583cc9cf96ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.9"}, {"id": "3d20549d-d795-3cec-a2ac-5fe8da2202e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "50fa00b1-12c9-3319-976b-bc41885a61de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <3b8f79af0e98f27b932b0b416e9c52b692d31ff9"}, {"id": "5f534931-6744-3672-ae35-6c14f318c6ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <646922a0379496154e8c8faca4f8e2fd9100cacc"}, {"id": "6111abb6-cf1a-3942-bd7f-b99b93536250", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <be65fa324640c7a95e30b146159a2be5cc73f22e"}, {"id": "7c22a7e1-fd29-3e71-9590-d892b29d4885", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.45"}, {"id": "96fdd4bb-315d-3359-bbee-b79e0567b61e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.104"}, {"id": "99e6649e-1afc-306e-b92a-bef458a21135", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ab36a296-a57c-3076-ab77-aba26c4327ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "cf9bef7c-be2d-3235-b1fd-81a92243cf4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.152"}, {"id": "fd2d0de8-eaa6-3581-aac2-5e21aef12a5a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <243d0187ec4c3837b9b0004f18d1068e46115760"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6d0412f9-b351-3f44-92f8-bab30ba80e28", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}